            "text": "OAuth Signature Parameter Mismatch: The parameters used to generate the OAuth signature (`params` map) do not match the parameters sent in the actual request URL (`encodeFoodSearchParams`). The `format=json` parameter is included in the URL but missing from the `params` map. This causes the signature to be calculated on a different set of parameters than what is sent, leading to signature verification failures (likely 401 Unauthorized) on the server side.\n\nRecommendation: Ensure that the exact same set of parameters is used for both generating the OAuth signature and constructing the final HTTP request URL. You should extract parameter building into a single source of truth.\n\nSnippet:         Map<String, String> params = new HashMap<>();\n        params.put(\"search_expression\", searchExpression);\n        params.put(\"max_results\", String.valueOf(maxResults));\n        String authenticatedString = oauth1Signature.createSignature(\"GET\", FOOD_BY_SEARCH, params);\n        String url = FOOD_BY_SEARCH + encodeFoodSearchParams(searchExpression, maxResults);"
